1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:02,640
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,557
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,400
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:19,020
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:24,217
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,737
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:29,497
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:35,000
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:40,420
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:42,680
One piece.

15
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:52,577
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:58,457
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:04,097
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

18
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:10,220
Is only legendary until
someone proves it real.

19
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,457
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times.

20
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:16,797
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

21
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:21,160
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

22
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:24,160
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

23
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:30,600
So come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

24
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:36,020
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

25
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:42,420
There's always room for you
if you want to be my friend.

26
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,880
We are, we are on a cruise.

27
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,700
We are.

28
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:58,122
Okay, at daybreak, the pirates will be
landing at this shore to begin their attack!

29
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:02,857
But the only way they'll be able to get
to the village is to go up this slope.

30
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:06,757
The rest of the shoreline is sheer
cliffs, so they have to come through here.

31
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,637
If we can fight them while they're
funneled into that narrow pass,

32
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:12,737
their numbers won't mean anything
and the village will be protected.

33
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:14,317
Alright, sounds pretty easy!

34
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,197
Talking about it is, but
victory depends on our strength.

35
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,737
What is it you guys can do?

36
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:20,040
I cut.

37
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,080
I stretch. I steal.

38
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:23,300
I hide.

39
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:25,517
Well, there's no way better to fight!

40
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,894
Just make it up funny!

41
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,180
Come on, calm down!

42
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:34,100
Ah, Klahadore, welcome back. How is she?

43
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:35,980
She's resting just now.

44
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:37,592
She was quite exhausted.

45
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:42,697
I leave town for a few hours
to tend to some errands,

46
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:44,604
and everything falls to pieces.

47
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:47,477
That Usopp certainly knows how
to cause trouble, doesn't he?

48
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:48,390
Yes.

49
00:02:48,473 --> 00:02:52,591
And on top of everything else he's done
today, he claimed you were a pirate.

50
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:55,160
I can't think of a more outrageous lie.

51
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:00,510
Indeed.

52
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,220
What's this here?

53
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:09,217
Well, that's a present, of course,
from Miss Kaya to you, Klahadore.

54
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:11,597
It's been three years since
you came to this mansion,

55
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:14,517
and this gift is to say
thank you for your hard work.

56
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,960
It's a commemoration of sorts. How nice.

57
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:20,817
The glasses you're wearing are always
slipping and you have to push them back up.

58
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:23,617
So the lady of the house custom
ordered a new pair for you.

59
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:27,406
Isn't she just the most thoughtful
young woman you've ever met?

60
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:31,120
How appropriate.

61
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:34,089
Tomorrow will be a day
worth commemorating.

62
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:41,940
It's a crescent moon tonight.

63
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:44,230
Huh?

64
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:47,980
It's on nights like these
that I truly feel alive.

65
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:51,880
My heart races and my
blood boils in my veins.

66
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:57,477
Clorador, what are you doing?

67
00:03:57,560 --> 00:04:00,678
Why would you do such a
thing to Miss Kaya's present?

68
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:03,400
Oh, I'll be receiving a gift, all right.

69
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:05,340
But it won't be glasses.

70
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:09,320
It'll be her entire estate. Oh!

71
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:11,037
What are you saying?

72
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:14,700
I suppose there's no reason to
carry on the act any longer.

73
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:19,480
In a few hours, the village will
be mourning the unforeseen tragedy.

74
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:27,520
Three long years I've
quietly waited for this.

75
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:29,070
Miss!

76
00:04:29,153 --> 00:04:29,983
You have to get out of here!

77
00:04:30,066 --> 00:04:30,896
Run!

78
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,080
Captain Django!

79
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:53,396
Captain Django, it's almost daybreak.

80
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,012
It's time to get moving.

81
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:57,754
Good morning, Captain.

82
00:04:57,940 --> 00:04:58,999
Good morning, sir.

83
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:01,560
You idiot.

84
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:04,897
Only the sun can wake me up
and live to tell about it.

85
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:06,333
Do I make myself clear?

86
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:08,060
He's in a really bad mood.

87
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,557
Mornings are the worst. Just look.

88
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:13,934
The moon is still up, so the
sun couldn't have woken me.

89
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:15,846
Now, which one of you did it?

90
00:05:16,180 --> 00:05:17,320
No apologies, sir.

91
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:18,774
We're very sorry, sir.

92
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:24,360
Good morning, gentlemen.

93
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:26,317
Wait, what's going on here?

94
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,937
He was mad just a second ago.

95
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:28,850
So what?

96
00:05:28,933 --> 00:05:32,137
He's in a better mood now, and that's all
that matters, so keep your big trap shut.

97
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:33,160
Attention, men.

98
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:35,720
Let's set sail!

99
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:43,959
Yep, I'm a genius.

100
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:47,597
There's no way they'll be able
to make it up this slope now.

101
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:51,617
All this oil we put here should keep them
occupied while we go to work on them.

102
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:54,537
They're going to be busy slipping and
sliding around like a bunch of idiots,

103
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:57,267
and we show up and beat
the crap out of them.

104
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:59,397
Wow, so that's your plan, huh?

105
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,310
That's right.

106
00:06:00,393 --> 00:06:02,917
I'm going to defend the village
no matter what it takes.

107
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,137
Let's just hope none of us slip on that
oil and end up down there with them,

108
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:08,577
because that would be like
sliding into a meat grinder.

109
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:10,540
Usopp, I gotta hand it to you.

110
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:12,777
You're pretty good at fighting dirty.

111
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:14,180
Of course I am!

112
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:16,497
There isn't anyone alive
who can best me with a

113
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:19,521
slingshot or beat me at
the art of fighting dirty!

114
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:25,720
It's almost daybreak.

115
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:27,102
They're coming.

116
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:45,500
We're here!

117
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:47,860
All right, men.

118
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:49,236
You know what to do.

119
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:52,580
Go ashore, crash the village,
head for the mansion.

120
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:53,660
Aye, sir!

121
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:57,200
Captain, there are already
two boats here. What?

122
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:59,800
Shall I investigate?

123
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,057
Leave them for later.

124
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:05,611
They don't look like treasure ships to
me, and we have a schedule to keep...

125
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:07,380
Where are they?

126
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:11,997
We were gonna fight the
sun's up. What's the deal?

127
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:14,160
Oh, maybe they overslept

128
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:21,260
Wait a minute, maybe I'm hearing things,

129
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:24,125
but it sounds like battle
cries from somewhere?

130
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:31,180
Yeah, I definitely hear them!

131
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:34,837
No, it can't be, what can't be?

132
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:37,744
And there's a shore just
like this to the north.

133
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:39,870
They went

134
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,360
We're at the wrong shore.

135
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:43,377
It's not good.

136
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:45,217
Well, this is where they
had their secret meeting.

137
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:46,653
So I just assumed, okay

138
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:50,577
We need to hurry before
they make it to the village.

139
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:51,490
Where is it?

140
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:54,637
You have to head directly north
from here if you run you can make

141
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:57,657
it in three minutes the terrain
there is almost exactly the same.

142
00:07:57,740 --> 00:08:00,505
So all we need to do is
stop them at the slope?

143
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:01,830
Oh, no!

144
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:07,117
If those filthy pirates are at the North
Shore, then they've already seen our boats!

145
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,617
They'll take our treasure!

146
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:11,460
I'll be there in 20 seconds! Oh, man!

147
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:14,366
My brilliant oil strategy
was all for nothing!

148
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:16,897
My precious treasure...

149
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:18,760
Hey, what are you doing?

150
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:19,817
Let's get out of here.

151
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:20,730
Yeah!

152
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:24,990
Help!

153
00:08:25,073 --> 00:08:25,903
I'm gonna fall!

154
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:29,020
Let go, you moron! Sorry!

155
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,190
Hello.

156
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:32,600
See you there.

157
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:40,860
Sorry, but you understand
the treasure's in danger.

158
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:43,489
That oil won't be a
problem for you, right?

159
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:45,160
That girl's gonna pay.

160
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:53,833
I swear all my life they'll
never set foot in my village.

161
00:08:54,260 --> 00:08:56,260
That Luffy sure has a good runner.

162
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:58,497
He's so far ahead, I can't
even see him anymore.

163
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:03,298
Run straight north!

164
00:09:03,780 --> 00:09:08,074
Those mongrels are in big trouble if
they so much as look at my treasure!

165
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:16,740
It's an ambush!

166
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:18,276
Somebody's up there!

167
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:21,060
We meet again.

168
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:35,860
I am the legendary Captain Usopp!

169
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:37,940
I've been waiting for you!

170
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,837
I wasn't supposed to
be the first one here!

171
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,657
He was running way ahead of me!

172
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:49,622
I can't handle these guys alone!

173
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,090
Crap!

174
00:09:55,173 --> 00:09:57,300
How am I supposed to get past this stuff?

175
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:02,680
The village!

176
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:04,097
That can't be right.

177
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:08,945
He said run north, and I ran in a coldish
direction, so I should be at the shore.

178
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:15,260
It's you. I remember.

179
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:18,357
You're one of the troublesome
brats who overheard our plan.

180
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:19,597
What do you think you're doing?

181
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:20,780
I'm warning you!

182
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,824
Leave here while you still can!

183
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:27,500
If you don't, my 100 million
crewmen will massacre all of you!

184
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:31,056
One hundred million?

185
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:34,120
Are we really supposed
to believe that? No way!

186
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:35,536
One hundred million?

187
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:36,570
Incredible!

188
00:10:36,653 --> 00:10:38,157
Captain, he's obviously lying.

189
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,037
Then it's time to call his bluff.

190
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:41,296
They saw through it.

191
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:45,420
That guy seriously thought he
could fool us. What's that?

192
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:47,893
You've been lying to us this whole time?

193
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,797
Captain Jango, take a look at this.

194
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:50,939
Oh, no, is it bad?

195
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:52,037
No, sir, it's good.

196
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:54,797
We searched those other ships and
found a huge load of treasure.

197
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:58,837
It's hard to say how much, but I bet
it's around five million berries.

198
00:10:58,920 --> 00:10:59,750
What?

199
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:01,780
Five million berries?

200
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:06,186
How in the world did those guys
get a hold of so much treasure?

201
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:09,260
I see you found my loot.

202
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:11,437
Well, you can have it.

203
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,837
You're just gonna let
us take your treasure?

204
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:14,750
That's right.

205
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:19,597
Just turn around and forget all about
this place, and the treasure is yours.

206
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:22,317
I didn't think people that
stupid actually existed.

207
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:25,106
At this point, he's just
embarrassing himself.

208
00:11:26,340 --> 00:11:28,720
Okay, do you know what a pirate is?

209
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:32,717
We're going to take this treasure, and
there's nothing you can do about it.

210
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:36,918
And there is no way we're turning
back until we get where we came for.

211
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,640
Well, yeah, that makes sense.

212
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:42,900
All right, then.

213
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:46,400
On the count of one, two,
Jango, you'll let us by.

214
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:49,576
It's that strange weapon from before.

215
00:11:50,860 --> 00:11:51,820
One, two...

216
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:55,998
Don't you ever try to get
my heart and treasure away!

217
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:00,430
My head!

218
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:03,217
Hey, who is this crazy girl?

219
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:05,297
Captain, this isn't the time
to be hypnotizing yourself.

220
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:07,733
We got a mission to carry out, remember?

221
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:11,397
That treasure boat is mine, and I'm not
going to let you have a single bearing.

222
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,310
Do you hear me?

223
00:12:12,393 --> 00:12:15,437
In fact, you better clear out, because
I'm coming down there to get it back!

224
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:16,497
That really hurts!

225
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:18,157
Who said you could give them my treasure?

226
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:19,070
You got what you deserve!

227
00:12:19,153 --> 00:12:20,897
I didn't give them the treasure.

228
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:22,937
I just said I would give it to them.

229
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:25,797
That's the same thing, and
I just saved your life.

230
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:26,710
Huh?

231
00:12:26,793 --> 00:12:28,877
I guess I forgot to
mention it to you earlier.

232
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:30,960
Don't ever watch his ring routine.

233
00:12:31,060 --> 00:12:32,700
That weirdo's a hypnotist.

234
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,430
Hypnotist?

235
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:36,640
So where's Luffy?

236
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:37,857
He's a fast runner.

237
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:39,597
I thought he'd be here way ahead of you.

238
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:40,510
I don't know.

239
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:44,012
He either got lost or he
chickened out at the last minute.

240
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:47,777
The only thing that could keep
him from a fight is getting lost.

241
00:12:47,860 --> 00:12:49,507
Right when we need him, too.

242
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:51,277
I'll go ahead and take command here.

243
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,477
I think it's about time you
go and kick their butts.

244
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:54,390
What? Me?

245
00:12:54,473 --> 00:12:55,303
What about you?

246
00:12:55,386 --> 00:12:58,317
I can't take on a boatload
of vicious pirates by myself.

247
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,576
That's just suicide.

248
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:01,517
What, like I'm gonna do any fighting?

249
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:04,997
Beneath this calm exterior lies
the abject terror of a coward.

250
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,817
Oh, so you think you're scared?

251
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:09,724
Well, I'm so scared I am
literally about to cry.

252
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:11,977
Please, your eyes are completely dry.

253
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:13,257
You'll have to do better than that.

254
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:14,477
Liars can smell their own.

255
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:15,857
That's just your upper lip.

256
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:17,137
I got beat up by...

257
00:13:17,220 --> 00:13:19,396
We don't have time for this nonsense.

258
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:22,297
All right, men, let's get to work.

259
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:24,439
Crush them and move to the village.

260
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,460
Here they come.

261
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:30,620
Wait, I know.

262
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:32,015
I have some Caltrups.

263
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:34,317
Those are just what the doctor ordered.

264
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:35,400
Let me have some.

265
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:40,160
You're gonna love this.

266
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:41,980
Caltrups! Help!

267
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:57,096
Nami, if you're still alive when I
get out of here, I'm gonna kill you!

268
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:06,380
Take that oil!

269
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:16,180
Now, how do I get to the
north shore from here?

270
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:17,880
Run straight north!

271
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:19,178
Run straight north!

272
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:21,020
Run straight north!

273
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:28,460
Which way is north?

274
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:35,960
Yes! We got him! Check it out! Here comes!

275
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:37,360
The lead star!

276
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:43,160
Bastard. Way to go.

277
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,137
You're quite the warrior after all.

278
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:47,437
Looks like you got this handled,
so I'll just take a break.

279
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:49,520
But you haven't done anything yet!

280
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:50,720
What is it?

281
00:14:51,420 --> 00:14:53,520
There are caltrops behind us.

282
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:55,050
Idiot!

283
00:14:55,133 --> 00:14:57,113
You dropped those things behind us, too?

284
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,120
Get out of the way!

285
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:08,690
Ha!

286
00:15:08,773 --> 00:15:12,798
Don't tell me you really thought you
were going to stop us down there!

287
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,600
Let's go, fellas!

288
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:17,468
Captain Kuro hates waiting!

289
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:23,920
You again?

290
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,220
Let go of me, you jackass!

291
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:27,617
You want some more?

292
00:15:27,700 --> 00:15:29,320
Here, have some!

293
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:30,577
Have a little more!

294
00:15:30,660 --> 00:15:32,057
I will never...

295
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:36,080
let you step foot in that village!

296
00:15:37,580 --> 00:15:40,640
All I did was lie like I always do.

297
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:47,477
See, today will be like every other
day in that sleepy little town.

298
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:50,137
Cause you and your cronies
will never set foot in it!

299
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:51,140
Shots?

300
00:15:55,940 --> 00:15:57,100
Stupid girls?

301
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:01,110
Treasure.

302
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:03,380
Are you?

303
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:07,200
Shut up I won't tell you again!

304
00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:12,160
We've wasted enough time playing pirates!

305
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:15,017
Quit bothering with him
and move to the village!

306
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:18,297
Or have you forgotten that this
is Captain Kuro's operation,

307
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:22,737
and he doesn't look favorably on his
well-laid plans being ruined by idiots?

308
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:23,920
He'll kill us all!

309
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:25,977
Do you understand that, you cretins?

310
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:27,060
He's right! Yeah!

311
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,791
Let's get to the village!

312
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:34,180
Don't go any further!

313
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:37,460
I said stop!

314
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,320
Turn back.

315
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:42,100
Don't take another step. Get off me!

316
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:51,820
Please don't kill them.

317
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:54,065
Just leave this village alone.

318
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:55,680
They're good people.

319
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:57,620
They don't deserve this.

320
00:16:57,860 --> 00:17:00,460
I love this place. Please.

321
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:18,660
What is this, Captain Django?

322
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:22,697
Nobody told us that killers like
those were going to be here!

323
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:23,920
It's about time.

324
00:17:27,740 --> 00:17:30,480
Is that the best those
pirates can dish out?

325
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,759
Yeah, I was hoping for a challenge.

326
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:34,750
And you!

327
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:37,697
After leaving me down there, you're
lucky I'm not kicking your butt, too!

328
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:39,280
Usopp, you big bonehead!

329
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:42,048
You never told me which
direction was north!

330
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:45,200
Who are these guys?

331
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:53,260
They're late.

332
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:56,520
I don't appreciate tardiness, not one bit.

333
00:17:56,900 --> 00:18:01,860
They know full well what happens to those
who are foolish enough to upset my plans.

334
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:11,287
Do they think they can
take their sweet time?

335
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:15,602
Well, if they have forgotten the
consequences of disappointing me,

336
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:18,060
I'll kill them all.

337
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:30,730
Wow!

338
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:32,500
That was great!

339
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:34,522
You guys are really that strong?

340
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:37,590
Mm-hmm.

341
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:38,937
Could you have been slower?

342
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:40,314
What took you so long?

343
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:44,297
You're the one who pushed me down
that oil slick so you could get out.

344
00:18:44,380 --> 00:18:45,217
It was an accident.

345
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:46,680
I slipped, you fell.

346
00:18:47,140 --> 00:18:48,897
At least one of us made it out of there.

347
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:51,337
That's better than both of
us being stuck at the bottom.

348
00:18:51,420 --> 00:18:53,240
It should have just been you!

349
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:55,037
Run straight north, he says.

350
00:18:55,120 --> 00:18:56,037
That's just great.

351
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:59,297
I mean, how am I supposed to know
which way north even is out here, huh?

352
00:18:59,380 --> 00:19:00,210
Shut up.

353
00:19:00,293 --> 00:19:04,077
You're the one who ran away so sure
of yourself, ready to take on anyone.

354
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:07,037
I just got so excited, I
started running, you know?

355
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:12,620
The sun rises high in the sky now, and that
means Captain Kuro goes very impatient.

356
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:15,929
Men, don't just lie there.

357
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:18,217
You can't tell me you're
going to let them win.

358
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:20,182
They're just a couple of idiots.

359
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:29,141
The fact is, we don't have time to
lollygag around here any longer.

360
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:33,437
If our enemy is strong, then we
must become stronger than them.

361
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:36,337
Here stare deeply into this ring now!

362
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:40,877
I will count one to jungle and after
that you will all begin to grow stronger.

363
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:45,372
Your wounds will heal and you will grow
stronger still so what is he doing?

364
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:47,920
It looks weird Looks like hypnosis.

365
00:19:48,220 --> 00:19:49,417
He's trying to convince them.

366
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:52,580
They're stronger than they
are like that'll work one

367
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:54,430
true

368
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:01,120
No way!

369
00:20:14,140 --> 00:20:16,840
That one guy completely
destroyed the cliff!

370
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:19,040
Now that's what I call power!

371
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:22,857
I always thought hypnotizing
people was a bunch of crap!

372
00:20:22,940 --> 00:20:24,257
That was just one of them!

373
00:20:24,340 --> 00:20:26,399
Imagine what the whole crew can do!

374
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:31,821
Now go, and strike down
all who stand in your way!

375
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,420
Hey, you guys, you might want to move.

376
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:48,153
Luffy, you and I will take it from here.

377
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:52,177
All right, then.

378
00:20:52,260 --> 00:20:53,090
What now?

379
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:58,060
Uh, Luffy?

380
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Don't tell me you let that
freak hypnotize you too!

381
00:21:12,740 --> 00:21:15,280
Oh, he really is a simple-minded idiot!

382
00:21:35,360 --> 00:21:39,280
Damn you, Captain Kuro, you made
one hell of a miscalculation.

383
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:42,851
These are not your average village idiots.

384
00:22:02,460 --> 00:22:03,620
Where's he going?

385
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,860
What is he doing?

386
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:19,780
That's right!

387
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:21,060
Tear it down!

388
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:24,740
He's going to destroy our ship!

389
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:38,560
Oh no, he's gonna crush
us with it, everybody run!

390
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,230
Run!

391
00:22:41,313 --> 00:22:42,280
Captain, do something!

392
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:49,020
One, two, jungle, you will fall asleep!

393
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:54,800
One, two, jungle!

394
00:22:55,800 --> 00:22:57,060
Ahhhh!

395
00:23:29,420 --> 00:23:32,217
Looks like those guys are probably
down for the count, don't you think?

396
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:33,130
I guess.

397
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,310
Maybe.

398
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:36,757
But Luffy's still trapped
underneath that cat.

399
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:37,670
Just look.

400
00:23:38,220 --> 00:23:39,640
Relax, he's fine.

401
00:23:39,860 --> 00:23:43,801
You should really worry about your
own injuries by the looks of it.

402
00:23:44,620 --> 00:23:45,914
Damn that little brat.

403
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:47,897
Now our whole plan's shot to hell.

404
00:23:47,980 --> 00:23:49,980
What am I gonna do with this mess?

405
00:23:52,540 --> 00:23:55,180
Captain Kuro sees this and he'll kill us!

406
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:58,577
Poochie, come check this out!

407
00:23:58,660 --> 00:24:00,660
There's some bad stuff going down!

408
00:24:00,820 --> 00:24:01,780
What the hell?

409
00:24:02,740 --> 00:24:05,000
I forgot we still have our trump card.

410
00:24:06,180 --> 00:24:07,137
Come forth!

411
00:24:07,220 --> 00:24:08,340
Meowban brothers!

412
00:24:20,740 --> 00:24:23,257
It looks like the butler
from Kaia's mansion.

413
00:24:23,340 --> 00:24:25,237
But it's so early in the morning.

414
00:24:25,320 --> 00:24:27,144
Why is he walking to the shore?

415
00:24:53,380 --> 00:24:55,657
Was in my grasp.

416
00:24:55,740 --> 00:24:58,120
And I wouldn't let go.

417
00:24:59,460 --> 00:25:02,097
La la la la.

418
00:25:02,180 --> 00:25:03,497
My only dream.

419
00:25:03,580 --> 00:25:05,677
La la la la la.

420
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:09,097
I won't stop chasing it!

421
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:11,600
Until it comes true.

422
00:25:13,500 --> 00:25:16,877
But if the world ever changes?

423
00:25:16,960 --> 00:25:19,957
I call out your name.

424
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:26,937
We return to the time when
everything's the same.

425
00:25:27,020 --> 00:25:33,597
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade.

426
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:38,980
Waiting for that one true dream?
